  "banks": {
    "_doc": "Bank character (plan 7E/7F/7J; tools/environment/banks.py, bank_props.py). Shore pixels get a soft character from a seeded low-frequency noise along the shore (char_noise_m, plus fine_mix of a 0.3x finer noise so the two banks of a narrow reach differ), biased by shoreline curvature (outer bends / convex water outline -> gravel and rock end, inner bends -> sedge end; bend_ref_m = bend radius giving full bias) and by bank slope (slope_bias_deg: flat -> sedge end, steep -> rock end). classes are bands of that value; values between bands stay plain (open access). rock is also forced where the band slope reaches rock_slope_deg or rock exposure rock_exposure. Sedge fades out on banks steeper than sedge_max_slope_deg. Inland banks: width_m band; sea coast: coast_width_m band, rock and gravel only (no sedge). Props: per rule, density (instances per 100 m2) per character field (optional require mask), own hash stream 'bank:<rule>', clusters of cluster [min, max] instances within cluster_radius_m; leaders and members are moved across the shore to a hashed distance inside shore_distance_m (negative = in water); only assets in in_water may stand in water, up to that depth (m). footprint_k = share of summed footprint radii kept clear inside a rule (0.8 default; low for reed clumps), face along_shore lays rubble on the contour, scale multiplies the asset scale range. groundcover: tall grass along sedge banks (tall_near_water at the water line, patchy, fading over tall_falloff_m), short grass cut on gravel banks. Placed after cliffs: no tree, prop or cliff moves. Editing this section does not change the placement seed (generate._seed_sha).",
